      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 39-year-old woman with long-standing anorexia nervosa was admitted to our hospital because of extreme weakness and cachexia. During a hyperalimentation therapy, she developed chest pain, revealing the electrocardiogram and cardiac enzymes a myocardial infarction of the inferior wall. We suggest that anorexia nervosa does not 'protect' against coronary atherosclerosis, and that some of the cases of sudden death could be related to myocardial ischemia."},
